spec: S03-08, S03-07, S03-13, S03-14

A BMP gets a web-safe PNG derivative (a second content-addressed blob, uploaded with the
original — the `new` size counts both) and its dimensions; the Sidecar lists the original only;
`pull --assets` writes the original bytes back (the re-push is `already v1`).

```console
$ annotary -p rowan push as-deriv.md
assets: 1 referenced, 1 new (3 KB)
as-deriv	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan push as-deriv.md --json assets
assets: 1 referenced, 0 new
{"assets":{"referenced":1,"new":0,"new_bytes":0}}

$ annotary -p rowan pull as-deriv --out out --assets
pull: 0 threads, 1 asset; 1 written, 0 unchanged
as-deriv.md	as-deriv.annotary	v1

$ annotary -p rowan push out/as-deriv.md
assets: 1 referenced, 0 new
as-deriv	[..]	already v1

```
